## 4. Notices and endpoint credit

When You distribute Materials, retain the Licensor's copyright and patent notices, include this license, and clearly state its expiration date. Mark changes to the Specification and reference software so readers can distinguish them from the Licensor's releases. Do not remove these notices from copies You distribute or conceal the expiration date from recipients.

When You supply an independently written implementation relying on this license, also provide recipients with this license and clearly state its expiration date.

Each web page You operate whose main purpose is to identify an AIRC endpoint, workspace, or realm and explain how to reach it must display:

> Uses the AIRC protocol, developed by Rafael Baptista. Learn more at airc.dev.

Link “AIRC protocol” or “airc.dev” to https://www.airc.dev/. A reasonably legible credit in the ordinary page content or footer is sufficient. Credit hidden only in source code, metadata, a separate legal page, or a closed menu is not sufficient. Markdown and plain-text versions of the page must include equivalent credit and the URL.

You may style or translate the credit without changing its meaning, and may use standard link qualifications such as `rel="nofollow"`. This attribution requirement does not itself require creating a web page or adding credit to individual protocol messages.

