## 7. If You break these terms

The notice, attribution, distribution, and naming requirements are conditions of the copyright and patent permissions granted here.

For an accidental notice or attribution failure, permissions continue for 30 days after You discover it or receive written notice, whichever comes first. Correct it within that period and permissions continue uninterrupted; otherwise they end at the end of that period. Any other material breach ends the permissions when it occurs. Ended permissions can be restored by the Licensor in writing. No correction period extends the preview's expiration date.

If You initiate or authorize a patent infringement claim alleging that implementing the Specification or using the unmodified reference software infringes a patent, Your patent permission ends when the claim is filed. A defense or counterclaim against a party that first sued You for patent infringement does not trigger this rule. Termination does not undo permission for earlier, properly authorized acts.

